A||N||3||jaguiler||Stock Manifold porting - what does that mean?||||1||
Z||000000||jaguiler||04-17-2001||04:05 PM||||Hi Everyone, <P>I have replaced my rear manifold with a new looking one from the junk yard.  I also picked up the front one as well.  I am planning on installing the front mani this Saturday.  Now these manifolds are stock.  How do I port them?  What is porting?  If it is what I think it is then can't I just do this with a drill and brush to cut down material inside the the holes?  Polish it up a little on the inside?  I don't mind doing the rear side either...I hear that is a good performance enhancement and since I am already replacing with stock ones why not modify?  Can someone explain please?  thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||209.246.221.97||reg||1
Z||000001||danny boy||04-17-2001||04:13 PM|||| Porting stock manifolds is nothing but grinding away the lip inside of the two rear runners. Look inside  and you'll see. That lip restricts airflow.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||04-17-2001||04:13 PM||||Here's some info:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007894.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007894.html</A><P>This page gives all the details and pics:<BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-exhaustmanifold.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-exhaustmanifold.html</A>  <P><BR>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 04-17-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000003||skitime||04-17-2001||04:56 PM||||This is one mod that I literally could feel at the gas pedal so by all means do it. I rewelded all welds with stainless steel and welded around the feet so the outside flange could be ported as well.||||reg||1
